WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.257
- [Reporter] Just showing
you again those pictures

00:00:01.257 --> 00:00:03.300
from earlier of Taliban fighters

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:07.320
behind the desk of the
Presidential Palace.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.680
- [Narrator] Taliban forces took over

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.200
the Afghan capital of Kabul on Sunday,

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.760
seizing power in the country
after just over a week

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.748
of a swift advances across Afghanistan.

00:00:16.748 --> 00:00:20.581
(man speaks foreign language)

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.070
- The speed of this Taliban takeover

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.090
has shocked anyone that I know

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.830
who has followed the
developments in the country

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.310
and shocked Afghans in Kabul.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.620
- [Narrator] As the
fighters entered the city,

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.720
President Ashraf Ghani fled the country

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.810
and by Monday morning,

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.120
people worried about
living under Taliban rule

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.713
flocked to Kabul's airport.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.730
- This is all happening far faster

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.750
than U.S. officials had predicted

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.720
and so a lot of questions on
Sunday about what went wrong.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.300
- [Narrator] Here's how
the Taliban's takeover

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.160
is creating new challenges
for the Biden administration

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.733
and an uncertain future
for the Afghan people.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:07.950
- It didn't take long
before thousands of Afghans

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.730
were swarming the airport

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.630
hoping to get out on evacuation flights.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.010
Some people had tickets
on civilian flights

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.400
that were later canceled

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.550
Overnight there was a lot of chaos

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.800
and at least three people
were killed by gunfire.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.160
We're not entirely sure by who,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.240
but it's the U.S military
that has taken control

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.750
of security of the airport.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:30.700
Meanwhile, the U.S. military
has sent extra American troops

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.810
to Afghanistan to help
facilitate these evacuations.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.610
There are currently roughly
6,000 American troops

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:40.830
either in Kabul airport
or on their way there,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.440
according to U.S. military officials.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.270
- I think an Afghan-inclusive government,

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.370
this is the demand, the will,

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:51.680
and the warmth of the
people of Afghanistan.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.690
- The Taliban have said repeatedly

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:57.800
that Afghan civilians have
nothing to fear from them.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.720
They also say the girls under the Taliban

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.830
will be allowed to go to school.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.300
But the fact is what we've
seen since they entered Kabul,

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.290
we've seen the Taliban raid NGO offices,

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.660
erect checkpoints throughout the city,

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:14.800
and people are concerned
that the Taliban will instate

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.350
the same kind of authoritarian rule

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.880
that they had in the nineties.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.580
We haven't seen large scale violence

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.850
against civilians in Kabul yet,

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.780
but there is already a very
pervasive sense of fear

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.613
in the capital.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.040
- [Narrator] As a Taliban advanced,

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.090
the U.S. was counting on Afghan forces

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.080
that it had invested
billions of dollars in

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.590
to train and build up
over the past 20 years.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.340
- [Reporter] Is a Taliban takeover

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.571
of Afghanistan now inevitable?

00:02:40.571 --> 00:02:42.433
- No, it is not

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.600
because the Afghan troops
have 300,000 well-equipped,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.140
as well-equipped as any army in the world,

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.840
and an air force

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.193
against something like 75,000 Taliban.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.383
It is not inevitable.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.030
- [Narrator] But Afghan security
forces largely surrendered

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.070
without a fight, so that by Sunday,

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.140
Taliban fighters were able to take control

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.903
of the whole country.

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:13.370
The Biden administration
stood by its decision

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.720
to exit Afghanistan.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.980
- We went to Afghanistan 20
years ago with one mission,

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.510
and that mission was
to deal with the folks

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.030
who attacked us on 9/11.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:22.760
And we have succeeded in that mission.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.593
- Perhaps the speed

00:03:23.593 --> 00:03:25.680
at which this happened wasn't predictable,

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.720
but the Taliban's takeover
was largely predictable,

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.350
and so a lot of questions now.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:33.050
If President Biden either
didn't know about that,

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:35.160
that's a problem with intelligence issues

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.050
or his own policy discussions.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.020
If he did know about it
and didn't care to do more,

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.870
then what does it say
about his willingness

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:46.970
to remain committed and
maintain his promises

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.413
to allies around the world?

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.770
- [Narrator] The Taliban's
rapid takeover of Afghanistan

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.570
also has implications for
the surrounding region.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:58.420
- It's the security implications
of Pakistan and Iran

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.380
and also all the bordering
countries are terrified

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.560
that, A, you have a refugee crisis,

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.830
people spilling over the borders.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:07.450
We're already seeing people trying to rush

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.783
out of the country in
fear of what will come.

